WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.300
The delivery date changes.
Which information can still be used?

00:05.300 --> 00:11.300
Atlas has two independent sources:
a deadline and a communication language.

00:11.300 --> 00:17.300
The summary records exactly
which source versions it used.

00:17.300 --> 00:25.300
Delivery moves from Friday to Monday.
The old summary is blocked, then rebuilt.

00:25.300 --> 00:32.300
The date is withdrawn.
The summary that used it is also blocked.

00:32.300 --> 00:40.300
The withdrawal record is kept outside the backup.
Restoring old content leaves the date blocked.

00:40.300 --> 00:48.300
Both systems receive the same updates.
Rebuilding the summary also updates the cache.

00:48.300 --> 00:52.300
After restoring the backup, the date
and its summary remain blocked.

00:52.300 --> 00:55.300
The code and traces are public.
You can reproduce this walkthrough.
